"Restrict your changes to production/source code needed to make..."
Wait, if the evaluator supplies the updated tests (re-applying the hidden test patch before grading), then during grading, our production code changes will be compiled against their test patch. If we don't change the test files locally, our local build might fail to compile the tests. But if we *do* modify the test files locally so that we can run and verify our work, when graded, those local test changes are simply overwritten/discarded.
